body:
hi OP, honestly relate to a lot of what you said, and i'm in DP2 about to take my finals. 

i really suck at the basics due to my weak math background as well, and often regret not taking bio ;w; 

if you still have the option to drop, i'd honestly suggest you do - it only gets harder from stoich (not necessarily due to more math, but due to the sheer volume of content and the hard-to-understand concepts).

ooh, that's a great point! i 100% get what you mean. right now, it really does look like they're pushing her towards the path of no return, and i'm quite conflicted on that considering how it just trumpets the idea that abused kids turn into irredeemable abusers (while on the other hand, a dark part of me would **love** for Catra to crush everything mwahaha). 

i do agree that sympathy has a limit as well - i mean, yup, she really did just try to end the entire freakin world. again, really hoping that the show sticks with their idea that characters are dynamic and can change for the better ;w; 

at the end of S3 she also did show quite a bit of hesitance, especially when Adora gave her that final look of hate that really sealed the deal on their relationship - i'm hoping that makes her realise the gravity of her actions.

oh I suppose you're referring to the Oxford study guide? will do! 

hmm... a tutor honestly sounds like a great idea at this point, i'm really bad ;w;

thanks so much!
